            <p>FaresChoice helps travelers compare available sailings, review pricing, and choose cruise options that fit their schedule and budget. It brings all the important details into one place, making booking simpler and more transparent. </p>

            <h3>Q. Do I need to plan flights and hotels separately for this cruise? </h3>
            <p>No, that is one of the main benefits of choosing Bahamas Paradise Cruise Line. The cruise itself covers transportation and accommodation, so travelers do not need to book separate flights or hotels for the main part of the trip</p>

            <h3>Q Will my deposit be refunded if my ship is late or cannot make it into port? </h3>
            <p>If your cruise ship cannot make port for any reason, your deposit will be fully refunded. If your ship arrives late and you miss your tour as a result, your deposit will be refunded. (Please note we can usually accommodate most delays.) </p>
            <p>We kindly ask you to keep us posted so we can keep our guides advised of your delay. If you cannot make a tour departure due to a ship delay or missed port, email us upon your return home to notify us, and your deposit will be refunded immediately. </p>

            <h3>Q: Can I spend US currency in the Bahamas? </h3>
            <p>Though the official currency in the Bahamas is the Bahamian Dollar, US Dollars are still king and accepted EVERYWHERE for payment. From taxis to stores, local vendors, bars, and restaurants. It is recommended to have bills of smaller denominations. </p>


